IMPORT prelude

-- Films Act 1981 (Singapore) -- the licence to import, distribute or publicly exhibit films in the course of business (s 6), what a
-- party political film is (s 2(2), (3)), films that must be refused classification (s 16), the unclassified-film and age-condition
-- offences (s 21(1), (7), (9), (10)), dealings in obscene films (ss 29, 30, 31), offences involving children and young persons
-- (s 32), party political films (s 33), composition (s 38B) and the Government exemption (s 40(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FA1981.txt. The deposit says it
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest annotations seen are [25/2018] and [30/2019]. The
-- ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the head of the deposit is out of step with the body from about s 28 onwards (it lists the obscene-film
-- dealing offence as s 28A, exemption as s 39A, composition as s 38A). This encoding follows the BODY's numbers: obscene dealings
-- s 29, possession s 30, advertising s 31, children s 32, party political films s 33, composition s 38B, exemption s 40.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duties and offences an importer,
-- distributor, exhibitor or member of the public meets. Not encoded: classification procedure and ratings (ss 13-15B, set by
-- Ministerial order), film content assessors (ss 19-20C), advertisement approval (ss 22, 22A), regulatory action against licensees
-- (s 11), appeals (ss 24-28), enforcement powers (s 34 and following), the Minister's prohibition orders (s 35), and corporate liability.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Films Act 1981 -- films`

§§ `6 and 40(1) -- licence to import, distribute or publicly exhibit`

-- s 6(1): "A person must not, unless authorised to do so by a licence or class licence -- (a) import any film in the course of any
-- business; (b) distribute ...; or (c) publicly exhibit any film in the course of any business." (2): fine up to $40,000 or 12 months
-- or both, and for a continuing offence "a further fine not exceeding $500 for every day or part of a day" after conviction.
-- s 2(1): "business" includes any business in Singapore "whether or not carried on for profit".
-- s 40(1): "This Act does not apply to or in relation to any film that is made, distributed or exhibited by or under the direction
-- and control of the Government."
-- The act is assumed to be one of importing, distributing or publicly exhibiting.
GIVEN `done in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by a licence or class licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a Government film` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 6 offence is committed` IF
        `done in the course of a business`
    AND (NOT `authorised by a licence or class licence`)
    AND (NOT `a Government film`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 6 maximum fine` MEANS 40000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `2(1), (2), (3) -- party political films`

-- s 2(1): "party political film" means a film "(a) that is an advertisement made by or on behalf of any political party in Singapore
-- or any body whose objects relate wholly or mainly to politics in Singapore ...; or (b) that is made by any person and directed
-- towards any political end in Singapore".
-- s 2(2): directed towards a political end if it contains matter that, "in the opinion of the Authority", is (a) "intended or likely
-- to affect voting in any election or national referendum", or (b) references to or comments on any political matter that are
-- "either partisan or biased" (political matter includes a current Government policy or "an issue of public controversy").
-- s 2(3): "none of the following films are to be regarded ... as a party political film": (a) news reporting by a licensed
-- broadcasting service; (b) information on election procedures and polling times; (c) a live record of a lawful performance,
-- assembly or procession not depicted "in a dramatic way"; (d) a record of a lawful event for participants; (e) a documentary
-- without animation, an accurate account of actual events, but not "reality" type programmes or dramatised; (f) a party manifesto
-- film without animation and dramatic elements, made by that party; (g) a candidate's declaration film, likewise.
-- The conditions inside each carve-out are taken as met when the carve-out is chosen.
DECLARE `Political carve-out` IS ONE OF
    `no carve-out`
    `news reporting by a licensed broadcaster`
    `election procedure information`
    `live record of a lawful event`
    `record of a lawful event for participants`
    `factual documentary`
    `party manifesto film`
    `candidate declaration film`

GIVEN `likely to affect voting in the opinion of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `partisan or biased political comment in the opinion of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the film is directed towards a political end` IF
    `likely to affect voting in the opinion of the Authority` OR `partisan or biased political comment in the opinion of the Authority`

GIVEN `an advertisement by a political party or political body` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `likely to affect voting` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `partisan or biased` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the carve-out` IS A `Political carve-out`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the film is a party political film` IF
        (    `an advertisement by a political party or political body`
         OR  `the film is directed towards a political end` `likely to affect voting` `partisan or biased`)
    AND CONSIDER `the carve-out`
        WHEN `no carve-out` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `16 -- films that must be refused classification`

-- s 16(1): "Despite anything in this Act, the Authority, the Committee of Appeal and an individual who is registered as a film content
-- assessor must refuse to classify any film that -- (a) is an obscene film; (b) is a party political film; (c) is a prohibited film;
-- (d) is against national security to be classified; or (e) contains any material prescribed." (2): such a film "is an unclassified
-- film".
GIVEN `obscene` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `party political` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `against national security to classify` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contains prescribed material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `classification must be refused` IF
    `obscene` OR `party political` OR `prohibited` OR `against national security to classify` OR `contains prescribed material`

§§ `21(1), (8), (10) -- unclassified films`

-- s 21(1): an offence if the person "(i) distributes or publicly exhibits an unclassified film; or (ii) has in the person's possession
-- a film that is an unclassified film, with the intention of distributing or publicly exhibiting the film" and "knows or ought
-- reasonably to have known that, or is reckless as to whether, the film is an unclassified film". (8)(a): $40,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 21(10): "A reference in this section to an unclassified film does not include a reference to an obscene film or exempt film, or
-- a party political film or prohibited film." Obscene and party political films are dealt with by ss 29-31 and 33 instead.
DECLARE `Film status` IS ONE OF
    `classified`
    `unclassified`
    `obscene`
    `party political`
    `prohibited`
    `exempt`

GIVEN `the status` IS A `Film status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as unclassified for s 21` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `unclassified` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the status` IS A `Film status`,
      `distributed, exhibited or held to do so` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew, ought to have known or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 21(1) offence is committed` IF
        `counts as unclassified for s 21` `the status`
    AND `distributed, exhibited or held to do so`
    AND `knew, ought to have known or was reckless`

§§ `21(7), (9) -- age conditions on a classification certificate`

-- s 21(7): where conditions on the classification certificate relate to distribution or exhibition "to persons below specified ages",
-- an offence to distribute or publicly exhibit the film to an individual "knowingly, negligently or recklessly in contravention" of
-- the condition; (8)(b): fine up to $5,000. (9): "it is a defence for the defendant to prove, on a balance of probabilities, that ...
-- there was produced to the defendant documentary evidence that might reasonably be accepted -- (a) as applying to the person ...;
-- and (b) as proving that the person was at least that specified age."
GIVEN `breached the age condition knowingly, negligently or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `documentary evidence of age was produced` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it might reasonably be accepted as that person's and as proving the age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 21(7) offence is made out` IF
        `breached the age condition knowingly, negligently or recklessly`
    AND (NOT (`documentary evidence of age was produced` AND `it might reasonably be accepted as that person's and as proving the age`))

§§ `29, 30, 31 -- obscene films`

-- s 2(1): "obscene" -- the effect of the film or any distinct part "if taken as a whole, such as to tend to deprave or corrupt persons
-- who are likely ... to see or hear the film".
-- s 29 (each "knowing or having reasonable cause to believe the film to be obscene"):
--   (1) makes or reproduces: $40,000 or 2 years or both; second or subsequent conviction $100,000 or 2 years or both.
--   (2) imports: $40,000 or 12 months or both; repeat $100,000 or 2 years or both.
--   (3) distributes, or possesses to distribute: $80,000 or 2 years or both; repeat $100,000 or 2 years or both.
--   (4) exhibits, or possesses to exhibit: "(a) to a fine not exceeding $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years"
--       -- with no "or to both"; repeat $100,000 or 2 years or both.
-- s 30(1): mere possession, no knowledge element: $20,000 or 6 months or both. (2): possession knowing or having reasonable cause:
--   $40,000 or 12 months or both; repeat $80,000 or 2 years or both.
-- s 31(1): advertising an obscene film for distribution or exhibition, no knowledge element: $5,000 or 6 months or both. (2): with
--   knowledge: $50,000 or 12 months or both; repeat $100,000 or 2 years or both.
-- Without knowledge, making, importing, distributing or exhibiting is not an offence under s 29 as such (0 below); the person may
-- still be caught by s 30(1) for the possession, which this function does not add.
DECLARE `Obscene dealing` IS ONE OF
    `making or reproducing`
    `importing`
    `distributing or possessing to distribute`
    `exhibiting or possessing to exhibit`
    `possessing`
    `advertising for distribution or exhibition`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A `Obscene dealing`,
      `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it obscene` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for an obscene film` MEANS
    IF `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it obscene`
    THEN `the knowing maximum fine` `the dealing` `a second or subsequent conviction`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the dealing`
         WHEN `possessing` THEN 20000
         WHEN `advertising for distribution or exhibition` THEN 5000
         OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A `Obscene dealing`,
      `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the knowing maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `repeat`
    THEN CONSIDER `the dealing`
         WHEN `possessing` THEN 80000
         OTHERWISE 100000
    ELSE CONSIDER `the dealing`
         WHEN `making or reproducing` THEN 40000
         WHEN `importing` THEN 40000
         WHEN `distributing or possessing to distribute` THEN 80000
         WHEN `exhibiting or possessing to exhibit` THEN 40000
         WHEN `possessing` THEN 40000
         WHEN `advertising for distribution or exhibition` THEN 50000
         OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A `Obscene dealing`,
      `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it obscene` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months for an obscene film` MEANS
    IF `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it obscene`
    THEN `the knowing maximum months` `the dealing` `a second or subsequent conviction`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the dealing`
         WHEN `possessing` THEN 6
         WHEN `advertising for distribution or exhibition` THEN 6
         OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A `Obscene dealing`,
      `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the knowing maximum months` MEANS
    IF `repeat`
    THEN 24
    ELSE CONSIDER `the dealing`
         WHEN `importing` THEN 12
         WHEN `possessing` THEN 12
         WHEN `advertising for distribution or exhibition` THEN 12
         OTHERWISE 24

-- Whether the court may impose both a fine and imprisonment. Only s 29(4)(a) (first conviction for exhibiting) omits "or to both".
GIVEN `the dealing` IS A `Obscene dealing`,
      `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it obscene` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IF
    IF `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it obscene`
    THEN NOT (`is exhibiting` `the dealing` AND (NOT `a second or subsequent conviction`))
    ELSE `the maximum fine for an obscene film` `the dealing` FALSE FALSE GREATER THAN 0

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A `Obscene dealing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is exhibiting` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `exhibiting or possessing to exhibit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `32 -- children and young persons`

-- s 2(1): "child" means a person "below 14 years of age"; "young person" means a person "14 years of age or above but below 18".
-- s 32(1): causing or procuring a child or young person, or having custody, charge or care of one, allowing them "to commit or abet in
-- the commission of any offence mentioned in section 29, 30 or 31": $80,000 or 12 months or both; repeat $100,000 or 2 years or both.
-- s 32(2): "If it is proved that a child has committed or abetted ... any offence mentioned in section 30(1) or 31(1), the person
-- having the custody, charge or care of the child ... is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have allowed" it.
-- The presumption reaches only a CHILD, and only the no-knowledge offences 30(1) and 31(1).
DECLARE `Obscene offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 29`
    `s 30(1)`
    `s 30(2)`
    `s 31(1)`
    `s 31(2)`

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a child` IF `age` LESS THAN 14

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a child or young person` IF `age` LESS THAN 18

GIVEN `age of the offender` IS A NUMBER, `the offence` IS A `Obscene offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the custodian is presumed to have allowed it` IF
        `is a child` `age of the offender`
    AND CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `s 30(1)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `s 31(1)` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `33 -- party political films`

-- s 33: any person who imports, makes or reproduces, distributes (or possesses to distribute), or exhibits (or possesses to exhibit)
-- any party political film, "knowing or having reasonable cause to believe the film to be a party political film", is liable "to a
-- fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years" -- again with no "or to both". Mere possession
-- without a purpose of distributing or exhibiting is not listed.
GIVEN `imported, made, distributed or exhibited it, or held it to do so` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it party political` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 33 offence is committed` IF
    `imported, made, distributed or exhibited it, or held it to do so` AND `knew or had reasonable cause to believe it party political`

§§ `38B -- composition`

-- s 38B(1): an enforcement officer may compound a prescribed compoundable offence "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of
-- the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000." (2): on payment "no
-- further proceedings are to be taken".
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `x` LESS THAN `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `the maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS `the lower of` (`the maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
